  "note": "The D455 in an IP65 enclosure (\"D456 is similar to D455 with an IP65 enclosure\"; IP6X dust and IPX5 water jets per IEC 60529, section 8.2.7). Poses: the body origin is the left imager's optical centre, the datasheet's depth origin (section 4.8.1); the right imager one baseline along -y, optical axes parallel to body x (the rectified geometry). The projector is placed at the baseline midpoint as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false; drawn but not dimensioned). Not stated: pixel size, distortion coefficients (\"Distortion <= 1.5%\"), subpixel accuracy: the lens model is pinhole, a labelled assumption. FOVs vary by about +/-3 degrees unit to unit (Table 3-49 note 3). max_range_m is the upper figure of the \"Range\" feature line (\"over\", \"varies with lighting conditions\"). Streams are the USB 3.1 Gen 1 tables; power_w is the \"All Components\" power at the Max Operating Mode (section 7.4). The RGB sensor (OV9782, global shutter, 90 x 65 degrees) has no stated offset: placed at the depth origin as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false). 6-DoF IMU (not modelled). Depth start point 4.55 mm (Table 4-17, as the D455). size_mm 124 x 29 x 26 mm (Table 3-53, shared with the D455; store page 124 x 26 x 29 mm), mass 116 g (Table 3-53). Both the depth and the RGB sensors can be synced by an external trigger (section 3.7.4). Store page: ideal range 0.6-6 m, min-Z ~52 cm, accuracy <2% at 4 m; mounting one 1/4-20 and two M4.",
